\section{Hamiltonian Structure of Annihilation-Triggered Ignition}

Let the ignition state of a micro-pellet be represented by canonical coordinates
$(q,p)$ describing compression radius, shock-front momentum, and internal plasma
state variables. TSSE requires that ignition evolve under a Hamiltonian of the form:
\[
H_{\text{ign}}(q,p) = H_{\text{ann}}(q,p) + H_{\text{fusion}}(q,p),
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
  \item $H_{\text{ann}}$ governs antimatter annihilation energetics.
  \item $H_{\text{fusion}}$ governs thermonuclear fusion energetics.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Antimatter Annihilation Hamiltonian}

Let $E_{\text{ann}}$ denote the annihilation energy delivered to the pellet:
\[
E_{\text{ann}} = 4.5\times10^7\,\text{J}.
\]

The annihilation Hamiltonian is:
\[
H_{\text{ann}} = \gamma_{\text{ann}}\,E_{\text{ann}},
\]
where $\gamma_{\text{ann}}$ is a TSSE temporal-symmetry scaling factor satisfying:
\[
\mathcal{T}H_{\text{ann}} = H_{\text{ann}}\mathcal{T}.
\]

\subsection{Fusion Hamiltonian}

With gain factor $Q = 320$, the fusion energy is:
\[
E_{\text{fusion}} = Q\,E_{\text{ann}} = 1.44\times10^{10}\,\text{J}.
\]

The fusion Hamiltonian is:
\[
H_{\text{fusion}} = \gamma_{\text{fusion}}\,E_{\text{fusion}},
\]
with $\gamma_{\text{fusion}}$ satisfying TSSE symplecticity:
\[
\mathcal{U}(t)^\top J\,\mathcal{U}(t) = J.
\]

