\section{Fusion Gain Manifold and TSSE Invariants}

Define the fusion gain manifold:
\[
\mathcal{S}_{\text{gain}} = 
\left\{(q,p) \mid G(q,p) = \frac{E_{\text{fusion}}}{E_{\text{ann}}} = Q\right\}.
\]

\begin{definition}[TSSE Fusion Gain Manifold]
A TSSE fusion gain manifold is a closed, invariant manifold satisfying:
\[
\mathcal{U}(t)\mathcal{S}_{\text{gain}} = \mathcal{S}_{\text{gain}}.
\]
\end{definition}

\begin{lemma}[Gain Invariance]
If $H_{\text{ign}}$ is TSSE-admissible, then:
\[
G(q(t),p(t)) = Q \quad \forall t.
\]
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
Since $G$ is defined as a ratio of TSSE-admissible Hamiltonians, and TSSE evolution
preserves Hamiltonian ratios under symplectic flow, invariance follows.
\end{proof}

This lemma ensures that TSSE engines maintain fusion gain stability across all
admissible ignition cycles.

