\section{Temporal Symmetry Constraints on Pellet Compression}

Let $r(t)$ denote the pellet compression radius. TSSE requires:
\[
\mathcal{T}r(t) = r(-t).
\]

\begin{lemma}[Temporal Compression Symmetry]
If $[H_{\text{ign}},\mathcal{T}] = 0$, then:
\[
r(t) = r(-t).
\]
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
Since $r(t)$ evolves under $\mathcal{U}(t)$ and $\mathcal{T}\mathcal{U}(t) =
\mathcal{U}(-t)\mathcal{T}$, temporal symmetry follows directly.
\end{proof}

This lemma ensures that TSSE ignition cycles preserve temporal symmetry even under
high-gain shock compression.

