\section{Symplectic Evolution of High-Gain Fusion}

Let $(q(t),p(t))$ evolve under the ignition Hamiltonian. TSSE requires:
\[
\mathcal{U}(t)^\top J\,\mathcal{U}(t) = J.
\]

\begin{theorem}[Symplectic Fusion Evolution]
High-gain fusion ignition under TSSE evolves symplectically and preserves
phase-space volume.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Since $H_{\text{ign}}$ is TSSE-admissible, its flow is symplectic. Therefore:
\[
\det(D\mathcal{U}(t)) = 1.
\]
\end{proof}

This theorem ensures that TSSE fusion ignition cycles remain dynamically stable.

