\section{Energy Conservation and Causal Closure}

TSSE requires strict causal closure:
\[
E_{\text{ann}} + E_{\text{fusion}} = E_{\text{total}},
\]
with no unexplained energy channels.

\begin{theorem}[TSSE Causal Closure]
If $H_{\text{ign}}$ is TSSE-admissible, then:
\[
E_{\text{total}}(t) = E_{\text{ann}} + E_{\text{fusion}}
\]
for all admissible ignition cycles.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
TSSE symplecticity preserves Hamiltonian energy. Since $H_{\text{ign}}$ is the sum
of TSSE-admissible Hamiltonians, closure follows.
\end{proof}

This theorem ensures that TSSE engines obey strict conservation laws.

